<title>JAPAN: Japan May tin imports down 15.1 pct year-on-year.</title>
<headline>Japan May tin imports down 15.1 pct year-on-year.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan imported 2,363 tonnes of refined tin in May, down 15.1 percent from 2,782 tonnes in the same month last year, the Finance Ministry said on Friday.</p>
<p>The imports (on a customs-cleared basis in tonnes) were as follows:</p>
<p>		    May 97    April 97	May 96</p>
<p> Total	     2,363     1,728	   2,782</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Malaysia	    620	 520	     660</p>
<p> China		 243	 284	     745</p>
<p>Cumulative imports in the first five months of 1997 were 11,003 tonnes, slightly down from 11,045 tonnes in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3 3432-6179</p>
</text>
